      },
      "lineNbr": 506,
      "author": {
        "id": 4159917
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-04T22:35:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently, it is happenning internally into BMPDecoder from image crate. \n\nThis is how I implemented in my first attempt (Patchset 10) in which I had a `try_read_row` public function in BMPDecoder, but this mixed set of methods was not accepted in image crate. I think that also part of the reason of pushback was due to having a large PR. With current implementation I think that if we expose the number of successfully decoded rows we can then get the when partial decoding due to UnexpectedEof happens. I will try to prepare a PR which should be quite small and hopefully there shouldn\u0027t be much pushback on accepting it.\n\nhttps://github.com/image-rs/image/pull/2758",
      "parentUuid": "3c89f8b8_fa2009b6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 499,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 506,
        "endChar": 9
      },
